{
  "_readme": "Build rules for the 'What could I build?' estimate. Setbacks come from setback_classes, chosen by the zone's family and the lot's size (the county brochure keys setbacks to lot size, not just zone). Families: AG = A-*a zones, RA = RA-.5a, RS = RS-* (by parcel sq ft), null = no setback data yet (no estimate shown). setbacks_confirmed stays false until Hawaii County Planning confirms the 2019 brochure is current. Per-zone coverage/height/dwellings must come from Hawaii County Code Ch. 25 with a citation; never fill from memory.",
  "setbacks_confirmed": false,
  "setbacks_last_checked": "2026-10-17",
  "sources": {
    "setback_brochure_2019": {
      "title": "Setback Requirements for Residential & Agricultural Districts",
      "publisher": "County of Hawai'i Planning Department",
      "revision": "Rev. April 2019",
      "url": "https://records.hawaiicounty.gov/weblink/1/edoc/140146/BLG_SETBACK_BROCHURE_REV2019.pdf",
      "notes": "Table column A (structure setback). Accessory buildings (sheds, water tanks, carports) observe the same yards. Irregular lots: the Planning Director specifies yards."
    }
  },
